---
title: Notebooks
layout: 'base.njk'
bodyClass: with-sidebar
---
<div class="notebook-layout">

{# A few notes to revisit, rotating daily through all of them (oldest-touched first), so nothing in the long list is forgotten #}
<aside class="visit-today">
<h2>Visit today</h2>
<ul>
    {% for post in collections.notes %}
    <li{% if loop.revindex0 >= 5 %} hidden{% endif %}>
        <a href="{{ post.url }}">{{ post.data.title or post.fileSlug }}</a>
        {% set excerpt = post.content | striptags | trim %}
        <p>{{ excerpt | truncate(140) if excerpt else "(empty so far)" }}</p>
    </li>
    {% endfor %}
</ul>
</aside>

<div class="notebook-main">

<p align="justify">This is a collection of my notes—some people call it a Garden—that I felt are worth keeping to recall information whenever I need it as quickly as possible. The material in these notebooks is mostly of my interest without any intention of being useful for others. Of course, in one lifetime, I could be an expert in maybe nothing. So it may offend other experts, for which you have my sincere apology in advance.</p>

<p align="justify">The topics are very diverse, ranging from myths, witches, and giants to philosophy and physics. In other words, whatever I found amusing, beautiful, strange, outrageous, weird, or otherwise noteworthy; things I want to learn and a list of references related to my research.</p>

<p align="justify">The format of these notebooks is copied from <a href="http://bactra.org/notebooks/">Cosma Shalizi</a> and I am deeply grateful for him to come up with such a nice idea.</p>
<hr>

<div class="view-toggle" role="group" aria-label="How to show the notes">
    <button type="button" data-view="categories" aria-pressed="true">By category</button>
    <button type="button" data-view="list" aria-pressed="false">Show all as list</button>
</div>

{# Grouped by the categories in the Index note (src/posts/index.md) #}
<div class="notes-view" data-view="categories">
{% for group in collections.categories %}
{% set popoverId = "category-" + (group.name | slugify) %}
<section class="category{% if group.unsorted %} wide{% endif %}">
{% if group.unsorted %}
<h3>{{ group.name }} <span class="count">{{ group.notes.length }}</span></h3>
{% else %}
<h3><button type="button" class="category-open" popovertarget="{{ popoverId }}">{{ group.name }} <span class="count">{{ group.notes.length }}</span></button></h3>
{% endif %}
<ul>
    {% for post in group.notes %}{% if group.unsorted or loop.index <= 10 %}
            <li>
                <a href="{{ post.url }}">{{ post.data.title or post.fileSlug }}</a>
                <time>{{ post.data | lastModified | shortDate }}</time>
            </li>
    {% endif %}{% endfor %}
</ul>
{% if not group.unsorted %}
<button type="button" class="category-more" popovertarget="{{ popoverId }}">Show all {{ group.notes.length }} &rarr;</button>

{# Full list of the category, shown as an overlay (native popover: closes on Esc or outside click) #}
<div class="category-popover" id="{{ popoverId }}" popover>
    <div class="category-popover-head">
        <h3>{{ group.name }} <span class="count">{{ group.notes.length }}</span></h3>
        <button type="button" popovertarget="{{ popoverId }}" popovertargetaction="hide" aria-label="Close">&times;</button>
    </div>
    <ul>
        {% for post in group.notes %}
        <li>
            <a href="{{ post.url }}">{{ post.data.title or post.fileSlug }}</a>
            <time>{{ post.data | lastModified | shortDate }}</time>
        </li>
        {% endfor %}
    </ul>
</div>
{% endif %}
</section>
{% endfor %}
</div>

<div class="notes-view" data-view="list" hidden>
<ul>
    {% for post in collections.notes %}
            <li>
                <a href="{{ post.url }}">{{ post.data.title or post.fileSlug }}</a> 
                <i>({{ post.data | lastModified | postDateNotes }})</i>
            </li>
    {% endfor %}
</ul>
</div>
 
</div>
</div>

<script>
  // Show 5 notes per day, walking from the least recently modified note through all of them
  (function () {
    var items = document.querySelectorAll(".visit-today li");
    var n = items.length, perDay = 5;
    if (n <= perDay) return;
    var day = Math.floor(Date.now() / 86400000);
    items.forEach(function (li) { li.hidden = true; });
    for (var i = 0; i < perDay; i++) {
      items[n - 1 - ((day * perDay + i) % n)].hidden = false;
    }
  })();

  // Switch between the category view and the full list; remember the choice
  (function () {
    var buttons = document.querySelectorAll(".view-toggle button");
    var views = document.querySelectorAll(".notes-view");
    function show(name) {
      views.forEach(function (v) { v.hidden = v.dataset.view !== name; });
      buttons.forEach(function (b) { b.setAttribute("aria-pressed", b.dataset.view === name); });
      try { localStorage.setItem("notes-view", name); } catch (e) {}
    }
    buttons.forEach(function (b) {
      b.addEventListener("click", function () { show(b.dataset.view); });
    });
    var saved = null;
    try { saved = localStorage.getItem("notes-view"); } catch (e) {}
    if (saved === "list") show("list");
  })();
</script>
